it/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">i</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\">size</a></span> := by get_elem_tactic)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/SInt/Basic.html#Int16\">Int16</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The element at the `USize` index `i`. It compiles to an inline load.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.uget","kind":"def","line":98,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.uget","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L98-L102"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.decSizeLt\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">decSizeLt</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Decidable\">Decidable</a> (<span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\">size</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize.size\">USize.size</a>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Decides `a.size < USize.size`, which holds for every array in memory, as for `usize`. The safe loops\nindex with `USize`, so their `csimp` proofs test the bound, with a fallback for the other case. At\nruntime this instance is `isTrue` without a test, so the compiler removes the test and the fallback,\nwhich would otherwise cost a `Nat` comparison and, when the fallback calls a fold, a closure for its\nfunction. This is the one unchecked fact behind those proofs.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.decSizeLt","kind":"instance","line":86,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.decSizeLt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L86-L96"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.decSizeLtImpl\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">decSizeLtImpl</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Decidable\">Decidable</a> (<span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\">size</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize.size\">USize.size</a>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"For internal use only.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.decSizeLtImpl","kind":"def","line":81,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.decSizeLtImpl","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L81-L84"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.toNat_usize_le\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">toNat_usize_le</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.usize\">usize</a></span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/UInt/BasicAux.html#USize.toNat\">toNat</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\">size</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"`a.usize` is at most the size, so it bounds the indices of loops that stop at `a.usize`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.toNat_usize_le","kind":"theorem","line":77,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.toNat_usize_le","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L77-L79"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.usize\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">usize</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The size of `a` as a `USize`. Since `USize` can address all memory, no array has more elements than\n`USize` can count.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.usize","kind":"def","line":69,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.usize","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L69-L75"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.usizeImpl\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">Internal</span>.<span class=\"name\">usizeImpl</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"For internal use only.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.usizeImpl","kind":"def","line":65,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.Internal.usizeImpl","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L65-L67"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">size</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The number of elements of `a`.","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.size","kind":"def","line":57,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.size","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L57-L63"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.mk_toArray\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">mk_toArray</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array\">Int16Array</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.mk\">mk</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span>.<a href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.toArray\">toArray</a></span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.mk_toArray","kind":"theorem","line":54,"name":"ScalarArray.Int16Array.mk_toArray","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-scalar-arrays/blob/ef15f198ef3e5fefe3f9b45b89a25772f75b1809/ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.lean#L54-L55"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./ScalarArray/Int16/Basic.html#ScalarArray.Int16Array.toArray_mk\"><span class=\"name\">ScalarArray</span>.<span class=\"name\">Int16Array</span>.<span class=\"name\">toArray_mk</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Ar